#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:1
msgid "6. Fused Multihead Attention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:3
msgid ""
"Attention computes a weighted combination of values across a sequence. In "
"transformers such as BERT and GPT, the input sequence produces query (Q), "
"key (K), and value (V) tensors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:7
msgid "Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax(Q @ K^T / √d) @ V\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:11
msgid "Where:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:12
msgid "**Q** (Query): \"What am I looking for?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:13
msgid "**K** (Key): \"What do I contain?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:14
msgid "**V** (Value): \"What information do I have?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:15
msgid "**d**: The embedding dimension of Q and K. This may differ from V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:17
msgid ""
"The softmax produces **attention weights** — a probability distribution over "
"positions in the sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:19
msgid ""
"This fused multihead attention (FMHA) kernel processes Q, K, and V in tiles "
"using online softmax. The compiler handles shared-memory staging, Tensor "
"Core mapping, register allocation, and memory coalescing. Elsewhere in the "
"project, FMHA is also called Flash Attention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:27
msgid "Attention score memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:29
msgid ""
"The intermediate attention scores matrix is quadratic in the sequence length:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:31
msgid ""
"Q shape: (batch, heads, seq_len, head_dim) = (1, 1, N, 64)\n"
"K shape: (batch, heads, seq_len, head_dim) = (1, 1, N, 64)\n"
"\n"
"Q @ K^T → shape: (1, 1, N, N)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:38
msgid ""
"![Standard attention requires O(N²) memory for the attention scores matrix]"
"(../_static/images/flash-attention-memory.svg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:38
msgid ""
"Standard attention requires O(N²) memory for the attention scores matrix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:40
msgid ""
"For N=65k, the scores matrix alone requires **4 billion elements**. Long "
"sequences simply do not fit in GPU memory with naive attention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:45
msgid "Row-wise softmax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:47
msgid ""
"Softmax requires access to **all values in a row** to compute `reduce_max` "
"and `reduce_sum`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:49
msgid ""
"let max_x = reduce_max(x, axis);\n"
"let exp_x = exp(x - max_x);\n"
"let sum_exp = reduce_sum(exp_x, axis);\n"
"let result = exp_x / sum_exp;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:56
msgid ""
"In standard attention, each row has N elements, so the entire N×N matrix "
"must be stored before computing softmax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:60
msgid "Online Softmax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:62
msgid ""
"Softmax can be computed **incrementally** by processing one chunk at a time "
"and maintaining running statistics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:64
msgid ""
"![Online softmax processes chunks incrementally, updating running stats](../"
"_static/images/flash-attention-online-softmax.svg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:64
msgid "Online softmax processes chunks incrementally, updating running stats"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:66
msgid ""
"When a new chunk introduces a larger maximum, previous results must be "
"corrected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:68
msgid ""
"Before: We computed exp(x₁ - m₁) where m₁ was the old max.\n"
"After:  We need exp(x₁ - m₂) where m₂ is the new (larger) max.\n"
"\n"
"Correction: exp(x₁ - m₂) = exp(x₁ - m₁) × exp(m₁ - m₂)\n"
"                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"                            what we had    correction factor (α)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:77
msgid "The algorithm maintains three running values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:78
msgid "`m`: Running maximum."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:79
msgid "`l`: Running sum of exponentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:80
msgid "`acc`: Running output accumulator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:82
msgid ""
"When a new maximum appears, all previous results are rescaled by "
"`exp(old_max - new_max)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:86
msgid "Memory Savings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:88
msgid ""
"![Flash Attention memory savings - comparing O(N²) vs O(N) memory usage](../"
"_static/images/flash-attention-memory-savings.svg)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:88
msgid "Flash Attention memory savings - comparing O(N²) vs O(N) memory usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:90
msgid "At any point the kernel stores:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:91
msgid "One Q tile: `BM × D` elements (e.g., 64 × 64 = 4,096)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:92
msgid "One K tile: `BN × D` elements (e.g., 32 × 64 = 2,048)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:93
msgid "One V tile: `BN × D` elements (e.g., 32 × 64 = 2,048)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:94
msgid "Running stats: `BM × 1` for max and sum (~64 each)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:95
msgid "Output accumulator: `BM × D` elements (4,096)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:97
msgid "Total: ~12,000 elements per tile, regardless of sequence length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:101
msgid "The Algorithm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:103
msgid ""
"For each Q tile (row block of the output):\n"
"    Initialize: max = -∞, sum = 0, output = 0\n"
"\n"
"    For each K,V tile (streaming through the sequence):\n"
"        1. Compute attention scores: scores = Q_tile @ K_tile^T\n"
"        2. Scale: scores = scores / √d\n"
"        3. Update running max: new_max = max(current_max, max(scores))\n"
"        4. Compute correction factor: α = exp(old_max - new_max)\n"
"        5. Rescale previous results: output *= α, sum *= α\n"
"        6. Compute new exponentials: P = exp(scores - new_max)\n"
"        7. Update sum: sum += sum(P)\n"
"        8. Accumulate: output += P @ V_tile\n"
"        9. Update max: current_max = new_max\n"
"\n"
"    Normalize: output = output / sum\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/06-flash-attention.md:121
msgid ""
"**Implementation note:** The code below uses `exp2` instead of `exp` as a "
"performance optimization — `exp2` is faster on GPU hardware. To compensate, "
"the scale factor is divided by `ln(2)` so that `exp2(x / ln(2), ftz::"
"Disabled) = exp(x)`. The correction factor `α` and softmax numerator `P` are "
"both computed with `exp2` using this adjusted scale."
msgstr ""

